        fp: "A customer visited an automobile showroom to test-drive a high-performance sports car. A salesperson employed by the dealership accompanied the customer in the passenger seat. While driving on a public highway, the customer became distracted by an incoming text message on his cell phone, looked down for five seconds, and ran a red light, colliding violently with a motorcyclist who had entered the intersection on a green light. The motorcyclist suffered catastrophic orthopedic injuries. The motorcyclist brought a negligence action against both the customer and the automobile dealership, asserting that the dealership was vicariously liable for the customer's negligence during the test-drive.",
